    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Two structural cross sections through the Kaibab monocline, Kane county, Utah are presented. The cross sections are divided into zones on the basis of the fracture type, geometry and distribution. The implications for flow properties of rocks are described. The relation of fracture type and distribution with structural position is studied to identify mechanisms of folding and fracturing, which can be used to predict the fracture distribution in similar settings at depth.",
